<body>
    <h1>Active Directory/Kerberos Configuration in IGEL OS 12</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>This article shows how to configure the options for Active Direc=
tory with Kerberos in IGEL OS.</p>
<hr>
<p>Menu path:<strong> Security &gt; Active Directory/Kerberos</strong></p>
<p></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper c=
onfluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image con=
fluence-content-image-border image-left" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=
=3D"89e62a3dc0e0d0fe383003b0b5a49b6a598f1ad9f873e3e5968f1a1be745ddd6" data-=
image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/7330=
2667/OS12_Actived%20Kerberos.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364=
680833&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"954" data-width=3D=
"1126" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73308=
959" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attach=
ment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"OS12_Actived Kerberos.png" data=
-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-con=
tent-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302667" data=
-linked-resource-container-version=3D"3" data-media-id=3D"717b52de-57c7-4f9=
5-a43e-28620e59b6f2" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"396"></span>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Enable</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91&nbsp;The Kerberos basic configuration will be carried out.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90&nbsp;The Kerberos basic configuration will not be carried out.=
 (Default)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Default domain (fully qualified domain name)</strong></p>
<p>This value must match the Windows domain on which the logon is to take p=
lace. The value must be entered in upper case letters. e.g.&nbsp;<code>EXAM=
PLE.COM</code>.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>DNS lookup for domain controller</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 In order to find the Key Distribution Centers (KDCs, domain co=
ntrollers) and other servers for a realm, if they are not explicitly indica=
ted, DNS SRV records are used. (Default)</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 The KDCs entered under <strong>Security &gt; Active Directory/=
Kerberos &gt; Domain 1&nbsp;</strong>...<strong>&nbsp;Domain 4&nbsp;</stron=
g>will be used.</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>DNS lookup for domain</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 In order to determine the Kerberos realm of a host, DNS TXT re=
cords are used. (Default)</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 The details under&nbsp;<strong>Setup &gt; Security &gt; Active=
 Directory/Kerberos &gt; Domain Realm Mapping&nbsp;</strong>are used.<br></=
p>
<p><strong>Obtain Addressless Tickets</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 The first Kerberos ticket is addressless. This may be necessar=
y if the client is located behind an Network Address Translation (NAT) devi=
ce. (Default)</p>
<hr>
<ul class=3D"childpages-macro">
<li><a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/p=
ages/73302307/Domain+Realm+Mapping+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-resource-id=
=3D"73302307" data-linked-resource-version=3D"5" data-linked-resource-type=
=3D"page">Domain Realm Mapping in IGEL OS 12</a></li>
<li><a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/p=
ages/73302313/Domain+Configuration+for+Active+Directory+Kerberos+in+IGEL+OS=
+12" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302313" data-linked-resource-version=3D"5=
" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Domain Configuration for Active Direct=
ory/Kerberos in IGEL OS 12</a></li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
